%% ASTRA — Sequence: Reactive Healing Loop
%% Render at: https://mermaid.live
%% Embed in docs/ARCHITECTURE.md

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Operator
    participant KPI as KPI Stream\n(Prometheus/Open5GS/E2)
    participant BUF as KPI Buffer\n(30-sample window)
    participant AE as LSTM Autoencoder\nAnomalyDetector
    participant XAI as AttentionExtractor\nXAI Attribution
    participant CLF as AnomalyClassifier\n5 Types
    participant TW as Digital Twin\nM/M/1 Simulator
    participant ENG as HealingActionEngine
    participant E2C as E2 RC Client\nDemo / Real
    participant GH as gNB / E2 Node
    participant WS as WebSocket Hub
    participant UI as React NOC Dashboard
    participant REDIS as Redis Streams
    participant PG as PostgreSQL Audit
    
    Note over KPI,UI: === REACTIVE HEALING LOOP (11.4s end-to-end) ===
    
    loop Every 1 second
        KPI->>BUF: Push KPI sample\n{dl_throughput, latency, bler, rsrp, ho, slice_util}
        BUF->>BUF: Maintain sliding window\n(30 samples × 6 KPIs)
        
        alt Window Ready (30 samples)
            BUF->>AE: window: np.ndarray[30, 6]
            AE->>AE: Scale via MinMaxScaler
            AE->>AE: Forward pass (PyTorch/ONNX)
            AE-->>BUF: total_mse, per_feature_mse, attention_weights
            
            AE->>AE: Update dynamic threshold\n3-sigma + consecutive counter
            
            alt Anomaly Detected (mse > threshold × 5 consecutive)
                AE->>XAI: per_feature_mse + attention_weights
                XAI->>XAI: Normalize to % contribution
                XAI->>XAI: Generate natural language explanation
                XAI-->>CLF: attribution_weights, top_cause, explanation
                
                CLF->>CLF: Map attribution → anomaly_type\n{CONGESTION, HIGH_LATENCY, PACKET_LOSS, SLICE_OVERFLOW, NOVEL}
                CLF-->>ENG: anomaly_type, confidence, top_kpis, reasoning
                
                par XAI Event to Dashboard
                    WS->>UI: ANOMALY_DETECTED event\n{type, attribution, explanation, anomaly_type}
                    UI->>UI: Update XAIAttribution bar chart
                and Twin Validation
                    ENG->>ENG: candidate_for(anomaly_type)\n→ HealingAction{action_type, params, rationale}
                    ENG->>TW: simulate_action(candidate, current_kpis, current_mse)
                    
                    TW->>TW: Derive λ, μ, ρ from KPIs\nρ = slice_util/100
                    TW->>TW: Apply action → new λ', μ'
                    TW->>TW: Compute new ρ', Lq, latency, throughput, BLER
                    TW->>TW: Project MSE via detector scoring
                    TW->>TW: improvement = (mse - projected_mse) / mse
                    TW-->>ENG: SimResult{projected_state, improvement, approved, queue_metrics, recommendation}
                    
                    alt Approved (improvement ≥ 20%)
                        ENG->>ENG: Enforce blast radius limits (prod mode)
                        ENG->>E2C: send_control(action_type, params)
                        
                        alt Real E2 Client
                            E2C->>E2C: Encode E2SM-RC Control Header (ASN.1 PER)
                            E2C->>E2C: Encode E2SM-RC Control Message (ASN.1 PER)
                            E2C->>GH: SCTP E2AP Control Request
                            GH-->>E2C: E2AP Control Acknowledge
                        else Demo E2 Client
                            E2C->>E2C: Mock success (1ms latency)
                        end
                        
                        E2C-->>ENG: {sent: true, sctp_transmitted, ric_request_id}
                        ENG->>ENG: Record healing_applied, update cooldown
                        
                        par Healing Event to Dashboard
                            WS->>UI: HEALING_APPLIED event\n{action_type, params, mttr, dt_approval, rollback}
                            UI->>UI: Update HealingLog + TopologyView
                        and Multi-Cell Coordination
                            ENG->>ENG: multicell.broadcast(source, action, params)
                            ENG->>WS: MULTICELL_BROADCAST event
                            WS->>UI: Neighbor notification animation
                        and Persistence
                            ENG->>REDIS: Async append to streams/hashes
                            ENG->>PG: Batch insert audit trail
                        end
                        
                    else Rejected (improvement < 20%)
                        ENG->>WS: ESCALATION event\n{reason: twin.recommendation}
                        WS->>UI: Show escalation alert
                    end
                    
                end
            else Normal
                AE->>AE: Append MSE to normal history
            end
        end
    end
    
    Note over Operator,UI: Operator can inject anomalies via NocControls\nGET /inject/anomaly?type=CONGESTION&cell=cell_001
    
